    "raw_difference": "C ECONNRESET vs Rust EOF on receive-stage denied TCP, with no DNS answer.",
    "claim_under_test": "After the implementation fix, no DNS data gives EOF and kernel-confirmed queued DNS bytes give reset, in both IPv4 and IPv6.",
    "finding": "Uncontrolled C reset vs Rust EOF was not only timing: admission-timing-01 proved Rust f1668e28 returned EOF with 41 bytes already queued. Root fix6506913 removes shutdown(Both), so plain close preserves the image boundary."
